  "result": "I made no changes to `next.rs`. The ticket can't be done inside its file scope.\n\n`%RegExpStringIteratorPrototype%.next` needs a RegExp String Iterator object, and nothing in the engine creates one. `RegExp.prototype[Symbol.matchAll]` (`reg_exp/prototype_symbol_match_all.rs:57`) still returns a not-implemented error where `CreateRegExpStringIterator` belongs. So `next` could never run on a real iterator. I also couldn't define the slot struct in `next.rs`. Without a constructor elsewhere it would be dead code, and lint suppression is architect-only (attempt 492 was rejected for exactly that).\n\nBLOCKED: `CreateRegExpStringIterator` must be implemented in `reg_exp/prototype_symbol_match_all.rs`, which is outside this ticket's scope. It needs a slot struct holding [[IteratingRegExp]], [[IteratedString]], [[Global]], [[Unicode]] and [[Done]], created with `ObjectKind::Native` and `%RegExpStringIteratorPrototype%`. `next.rs` can then be written against that struct.",
